    "html": "<p>A sealed container holds a fixed mass of a gas that behaves ideally. The pressure of the gas is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and its volume is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span>. If the absolute temperature of the gas is tripled and the volume is increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.5V\"></span>, what is the new pressure of the gas?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.5P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.0P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.5P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0P\"></span></p></li></ol>"
